List Intersection
=================

Write a function:

    def list_intersection(lists: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]

Return the numbers that appear in ALL of the inner lists, sorted in ascending
order, without duplicates.

Examples:
    list_intersection([[5, 4, 3], [2, 1, 3], [2, 1, 3]]) -> [3]
    list_intersection([[5, 4, 3], [2, 1, 6], [7, 0, 9]]) -> []
    list_intersection([[1, 2], [2, 3]]) -> [2]
    list_intersection([]) -> []
